family: net-snmp
what: trap
transport: v3
address: 192.0.2.10
verification: tested
reference: net-snmp manual pages: snmpd.conf(5) (trap2sink, trapsess), snmp.conf(5) (defCommunity, defSecurityName, defAuthType…), snmptrap(1)
does: Makes snmpd send its traps to Woodshed (SNMPv3), and gives a test trap to send with snmptrap.
check: Search Events for type Traps: the trap snmpd sends at start (coldStart) and the test trap each appear once; `woodshed snmp status` counts them.
placeholders: <V3-USER> <AUTH-PASSPHRASE> <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
addresses: 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- Add the same user in Woodshed first: Settings → SNMP → v3 users, name <V3-USER>, SHA-256 and AES-128, with the same passphrases (at least 8 characters each).
- Keep snmpd.conf readable by root only: it holds the passphrases.
- The test trap's OID is under the documentation enterprise number (32473), so it can't be mistaken for a real alarm.
---- part file "/etc/snmp/snmpd.conf": Add to the agent's configuration, then restart snmpd (sudo systemctl restart snmpd); it sends a trap when it starts
# Woodshed: send traps (SNMPv3).
trapsess -v 3 -u <V3-USER> -l authPriv -a SHA-256 -A <AUTH-PASSPHRASE> -x AES -X <PRIV-PASSPHRASE> udp:192.0.2.10:162
---- part file "~/.snmp/snmp.conf": For the test trap: snmptrap reads its user and passphrases from this file, not the command line
defSecurityName <V3-USER>
defSecurityLevel authPriv
defAuthType SHA-256
defAuthPassphrase <AUTH-PASSPHRASE>
defPrivType AES
defPrivPassphrase <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
---- part command "": Send a test trap
snmptrap -v 3 udp:192.0.2.10:162 '' 1.3.6.1.4.1.32473.1.0.1 1.3.6.1.4.1.32473.1.1.1.0 s "Test trap for Woodshed from $(hostname)"
==== text
# /etc/snmp/snmpd.conf: Add to the agent's configuration, then restart snmpd (sudo systemctl restart snmpd); it sends a trap when it starts
# Woodshed: send traps (SNMPv3).
trapsess -v 3 -u <V3-USER> -l authPriv -a SHA-256 -A <AUTH-PASSPHRASE> -x AES -X <PRIV-PASSPHRASE> udp:192.0.2.10:162

# ~/.snmp/snmp.conf: For the test trap: snmptrap reads its user and passphrases from this file, not the command line
defSecurityName <V3-USER>
defSecurityLevel authPriv
defAuthType SHA-256
defAuthPassphrase <AUTH-PASSPHRASE>
defPrivType AES
defPrivPassphrase <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>

# Send a test trap
snmptrap -v 3 udp:192.0.2.10:162 '' 1.3.6.1.4.1.32473.1.0.1 1.3.6.1.4.1.32473.1.1.1.0 s "Test trap for Woodshed from $(hostname)"
